<emu-clause id="sec-properties-of-the-string-prototype-object" number="22.1.3">
  <h1>Properties of the String Prototype Object</h1>

  <emu-clause id="sec-string.prototype.trim" type="built-in function" number="32">
    <h1>String.prototype.trim ( <ins>[ _characters_ ]</ins> )</h1>
    <p>This method interprets a String value as a sequence of UTF-16 encoded code points, as described in <emu-xref href="#sec-ecmascript-language-types-string-type"></emu-xref>.</p>
    <p>It performs the following steps when called:</p>
    <emu-alg>
      1. Let _thisValue_ be the *this* value.
      1. Return ? TrimString(_thisValue_, ~start+end~<ins>, _characters_</ins>).
    </emu-alg>
    <emu-note>
      <p>This method is intentionally generic; it does not require that its *this* value be a String object. Therefore, it can be transferred to other kinds of objects for use as a method.</p>
    </emu-note>

    <emu-clause id="sec-trimstring" type="abstract operation">
      <h1>
        TrimString (
          _string_: an ECMAScript language value,
          _where_: ~start~, ~end~, or ~start+end~,
          <ins>optional _characters_: a String,</ins>
        ): either a normal completion containing a String or a throw completion
      </h1>
      <dl class="header">
        <dt>description</dt>
        <dd>It interprets _string_ as a sequence of UTF-16 encoded code points, as described in <emu-xref href="#sec-ecmascript-language-types-string-type"></emu-xref>.</dd>
      </dl>
      <emu-alg>
        1. Perform ? RequireObjectCoercible(_string_).
        1. Let _str_ be ? ToString(_string_).
        1. <ins>If _characters_ is *undefined*, then</ins>
          1. <ins>Let _trimSet_ be the set of code points that is the union of |WhiteSpace| and |LineTerminator|.</ins>
        1. <ins>Else,</ins>
          1. <ins>If _characters_ is not a String, throw a *TypeError* exception.</ins>
          1. <ins>Let _trimSet_ be the set of unique code points in _characters_.</ins>
        1. If _where_ is ~start~, then
          1. Let _trimmedString_ be the String value that is a copy of _str_ with leading <del>white space</del><ins>code points in _trimSet_</ins> removed.
        1. Else if _where_ is ~end~, then
          1. Let _trimmedString_ be the String value that is a copy of _str_ with trailing <del>white space</del><ins>code points in _trimSet_</ins> removed.
        1. Else,
          1. Assert: _where_ is ~start+end~.
          1. Let _trimmedString_ be the String value that is a copy of _str_ with both leading and trailing <del>white space</del><ins>code points in _trimSet_</ins> removed.
        1. Return _trimmedString_.
      </emu-alg>
      <p><del>The definition of white space is the union of |WhiteSpace| and |LineTerminator|.</del> When determining whether a Unicode code point is in Unicode general category “Space_Separator” (“Zs”), code unit sequences are interpreted as UTF-16 encoded code point sequences as specified in <emu-xref href="#sec-ecmascript-language-types-string-type"></emu-xref>.</p>
    </emu-clause>
  </emu-clause>

  <emu-clause id="sec-string.prototype.trimend" type="built-in function">
    <h1>String.prototype.trimEnd ( <ins>[ _characters_ ]</ins> )</h1>
    <p>This method interprets a String value as a sequence of UTF-16 encoded code points, as described in <emu-xref href="#sec-ecmascript-language-types-string-type"></emu-xref>.</p>
    <p>It performs the following steps when called:</p>
    <emu-alg>
      1. Let _str_ be the *this* value.
      1. Return ? TrimString(_str_, ~end~<ins>, _characters_</ins>).
    </emu-alg>
    <emu-note>
      <p>This method is intentionally generic; it does not require that its *this* value be a String object. Therefore, it can be transferred to other kinds of objects for use as a method.</p>
    </emu-note>
  </emu-clause>

  <emu-clause id="sec-string.prototype.trimstart" type="built-in function">
    <h1>String.prototype.trimStart ( <ins>[ _characters_ ]</ins> )</h1>
    <p>This method interprets a String value as a sequence of UTF-16 encoded code points, as described in <emu-xref href="#sec-ecmascript-language-types-string-type"></emu-xref>.</p>
    <p>It performs the following steps when called:</p>
    <emu-alg>
      1. Let _str_ be the *this* value.
      1. Return ? TrimString(_str_, ~start~<ins>, _characters_</ins>).
    </emu-alg>
    <emu-note>
      <p>This method is intentionally generic; it does not require that its *this* value be a String object. Therefore, it can be transferred to other kinds of objects for use as a method.</p>
    </emu-note>
  </emu-clause>
</emu-clause>
